# builtin-is-contractive
--- uses: ["core"]
# returns false for a TypeNode.RecursiveRef variant.
# This is Case 1 of the contractiveness algorithm: a bare RecursiveRef at the root
# represents the non-contractive type μa.a (direct self-reference, no structural wrapper).
# builtin-variant constructs the Variant value; builtin-is-contractive checks it.
# Both are internal builtins, accessible at runtime but not registered in the type env.
[ref-node: [builtin-variant "TypeNode.RecursiveRef" [name: "a"]]]
[result: [builtin-is-contractive ref-node]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(false)})
